{"title":"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution (Pythagorean Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If circular arcs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> have centers at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, then there exists a circle tangent to both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/b/d0b17acc99a99a0d00c2b288db5277ca51c7cfd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overarc {AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f997f2e439fbb9578ac4d715bc866bbea93ebc2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overarc{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"20\" />, and to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. If the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f997f2e439fbb9578ac4d715bc866bbea93ebc2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overarc{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then the circumference of the circle is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9af3929a28ff1ea51952e3d9e729aaa0f0869a15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] label(&quot;A&quot;, (0,0), W); label(&quot;B&quot;, (64,0), E); label(&quot;C&quot;, (32, 32*sqrt(3)), N); draw(arc((0,0),64,0,60)); draw(arc((64,0),64,120,180)); draw((0,0)--(64,0));  draw(circle((32, 24), 24)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"212\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe3876a48b99ce85514e4f1269c67acc97a4234b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf {(A)}\\ 24 \\qquad \\textbf {(B)}\\ 25 \\qquad \\textbf {(C)}\\ 26 \\qquad \\textbf {(D)}\\ 27 \\qquad \\textbf {(E)}\\ 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28Pythagorean_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\">Solution (Pythagorean Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (Pythagorean Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/7198a03dcc873ce84ef122fb51947cbd9cc09310.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] label(&quot;A&quot;, (0,0), W); label(&quot;B&quot;, (64,0), E); label(&quot;C&quot;, (32, 32*sqrt(3)), N); label(&quot;O&quot;, (32, 24), NW); label(&quot;M&quot;, (32,0), S); label(&quot;N&quot;, (51.2, 38.4), NE); dot((32, 24)); draw(arc((0,0),64,0,60)); draw(arc((64,0),64,120,180)); draw((0,0)--(64,0)); draw((0,0)--(51.2,38.4)); draw((32,24)--(32,0)); draw((0,0)--(32,32*sqrt(3))--(64,0), dashed); draw(circle((32, 24), 24)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"222\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equilateral, arcs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of a circle.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the radius of these arcs.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76faa3f1d4d3c2a47aa24b19487dc89e7c889c90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}(2\\pi R) = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c050e2cc41a66053d1df4ac932580932c6bf452.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\frac{36}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the inscribed circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afbaf74a3151d52433028847a24f7f3f02faec49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = \\frac{R}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0c8c40caeca09a92620afe16be18d5db28b9f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a869a404bb1006b5ac39c73f39514796a854f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO = R-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" />.  By the Pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/4/e64d900f148503b383d438f84afd8b00567b63e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM^2 + OM^2 = AO^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2ef19082b977f957b52362c526d0adbb4aff27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{R}{2}\\right)^2 + r^2 = (R-r)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"182\" height=\"48\" />.  Solving this equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b0051625c3f162bdd6fc3589a127e331a38471e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{3R}{4} = \\frac{27}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"39\" />, so the circumference of the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/954d2ae888fe9fcf5b914a56c308964cb09ae0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2{\\pi}\\left(\\frac{27}{2\\pi}\\right)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"164\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PuVeGNHIkDg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PuVeGNHIkDg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=3466\">https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=3466</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QyeaoEtgu-Y\">https://youtu.be/QyeaoEtgu-Y</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 12\">2000 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017193600\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.080 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 281/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7187/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.476      1 -total\n 62.70%   10.330      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 35.39%    5.831      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6142:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017193600 and revision id 283582. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}